# Accessibility first

This app helps people judge how usable a Pittsburgh place is: walking, wheelchair access, ramps, hills, restrooms, and similar barriers. Reviews support that. They are not the product.

- Lead UI with access facts (walk, wheelchair, ramps). Ratings and write-ups should describe access, not only vibe.
- New landmarks need a map-picked point and access fields (walk, wheelchair, ramps).
- Do not add tourist-only features that hide access information.
- Prefer concrete access language: "step-free," "steep curb," "ramp at the side door."

```jsx
// ❌ BAD
<p>{place.description}</p>

// ✅ GOOD
<AccessFacts access={accessibilityFor(place)} />
<p>{place.accessibility.notes}</p>
```
